Description: rsync backups from Linux servers to a Synology NAS
 rSynBackTux backs up a Linux server to a Synology NAS over the NAS built-in
 rsync daemon. No agent and no additional software is needed on the NAS side,
 only the rsync service and a shared folder configured as a network backup
 destination.
 .
 The package ships the backup runner, a systemd service and timer, a logrotate
 snippet and the rsync exclude list. Run "rsynbacktux-setup" once after the
 installation to configure the NAS host, the rsync module, the credentials and
 the schedule; everything else is read from /etc/rsynbacktux/backup.conf at
 run time.
 .
 Backups are incremental, guarded against parallel runs and rsync exit code 24
 ("vanished files") is treated as success, which makes unattended runs on a
 live system reliable.

